@format 1
@id media-preview.in-audio
@title In Audio
@section Media preview
@area In Audio
@entry audio-path-change
@summary Show Audio-specific selected-path preview loading, including the conditional current-plan save and immediate restore around PViewerSourceOpen.
@related media-selection.common.files-selection, media-preview.common.viewer-gate, media-loading.in-audio
@tag media
@tag preview
@tag audio

@alias audio = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PAudioTab
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer

[audio-path-change] Audio Files current-path event <input>
~ This starts when the selected file changes in the Audio tab.
[Technical explanation]
= PListPathChange synchronously delivered a current path to PAudioPathShow.
> audio-path-result

[audio-path-result] Audio selected-path adapter <decision>
~ The Audio tab decides what to do with the newly selected media path.
[Technical explanation]
- Ignore blank paths; for a nonblank path, PAudioPathShow first calls PAudioPlanSave before requesting preview media @ audio.PAudioPathShow(...)
? "Nonblank current path" > audio-save-gate
? "Blank current path" > audio-no-request

[audio-save-gate] Current Audio plan needs saving <decision>
~ The program checks whether the current Audio settings need to be saved before switching media.
[Technical explanation]
- PAudioPlanSave returns without writing while plan loading is active, when no viewer source is committed, when that source is locked, or when the current plan is inactive and no saved plan exists; otherwise it saves the current plan @ audio.PAudioPlanSave(...)
? "Save conditions met" > audio-save
? "Save skipped" > audio-save-skipped

[audio-save] Save current committed source plan <process>
~ The program saves the settings for the media that is currently active.
[Technical explanation]
- Save the current Audio work plan for the committed viewer source and update persistent carried Audio state @ audio.PAudioPlanSave(...)
> audio-save-join

[audio-save-skipped] Current-plan write skipped <junction>
> audio-save-join

[audio-save-join] Audio pre-request paths converge <junction>
> audio-viewer-call

[audio-no-request] Audio preview request omitted <output>
~ This path ends with audio preview request omitted.
[Technical explanation]
= Audio does not call PViewerSourceOpen for a blank current path.

[audio-viewer-call] Request selected source in viewer <process>
~ This step handles request selected source in viewer.
[Technical explanation]
- Call PViewerSourceOpen for the requested path; the shared Viewer gate runs synchronously and backend preview work may continue asynchronously @ audio.PAudioPathShow(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerSourceOpen(...)
> immediate-restore

[immediate-restore] Restore against currently committed viewer source <process>
~ This step handles restore against currently current viewer source.
[Technical explanation]
- Immediately after PViewerSourceOpen returns, call PAudioPlanRestore; it reads PViewerSourcePath and duration, which do not change to the requested source until a later successful viewer commit @ audio.PAudioPlanRestore(...)
  @ property viewer.PViewerSourcePath
! On a normal asynchronous request this usually restores against the previous committed source, or null on an initially empty viewer. Audio has no PViewerMediaChange subscription that automatically reruns PAudioPlanRestore after the new preview later commits.
> audio-transition-complete

[audio-transition-complete] Immediate Audio preview transition finished <output>
~ This path ends with immediate Audio preview transition finished.
[Technical explanation]
= PAudioPathShow has returned while the requested preview load may still be running independently.
